keywords:
  - AI security
  - autonomous agents
  - long-term memory
  - memory poisoning
  - prompt injection
  - retrieval-augmented generation
abstract: >-
  MemShield is an experimental three-layer middleware architecture for reducing
  persistent memory poisoning in stateful autonomous AI agents through
  cryptographic provenance, trust-weighted retrieval with temporal decay, and
  semantic contradiction detection. Reported results are based on a custom
  simulation harness and have not been independently peer reviewed.
